            <ArticleTitle>Note: Retrofitting an analog spectrometer for high resolving power in NUV-NIR.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1063/1.5009490</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We demonstrate how an older spectrometer designed for photographic films can be efficiently retrofitted with a narrow laser-cut slit and a modern μm-pixel-size imaging CMOS camera, yielding sub-pm resolution in the broad near ultraviolet to near infrared (NUV-NIR) spectral range. Resolving power approaching 106 is achieved. Such digital retrofitting of an analog instrument is practical for research and teaching laboratories.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
